# Search-tool exclusions — honoured by ripgrep, fd, and most agent tooling.
#
# These are generated artefacts that are gitignored but still sit in the working
# tree, so `git status` stays quiet while recursive search walks straight into them.
#
# graphify-out/ is the dangerous one. graph.json indexes the source, so it matches
# ordinary identifiers ("sessions", "extractPayerName", "supabase"), and graph.html
# holds a SINGLE ~1.4 MB line. An unscoped `rg <identifier>` therefore returns a
# megabyte-long line, which is enough on its own to exhaust an agent's context
# window. Observed 2026-07-29: three subagents died this way before the cause was
# found — it surfaces as a generic autocompact/API error, so it reads like a model
# problem rather than a repo problem.
#
# NOTE: plain `grep -r` does NOT honour this file. Use ripgrep, or pass
#   --exclude-dir={graphify-out,node_modules,.git}
graphify-out/
node_modules/
